{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user wants me to implement a `solve(case)` function that filters API calls based on Toolformer-style loss filtering. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. A call is accepted if: `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics in original order\n\nThe response must be a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source.\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\n- `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n- `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n- Accept if `parseable` and `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n\nFor the diagnostics, I need to include per-call info like gain, normalized_gain, accepted/rejected.\n\nThe contract mentions:\n- `normalized_weights` - normalizing by prediction tokens\n- `stronger_counterfactual` - using loss_without - loss_with (the counterfactual of having the call vs not)\n- `inclusive_threshold` - `\u003e=` threshold (inclusive)\n- `stable_order` - preserve source order\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    import math\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be numeric\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    accepted_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        # Validate required fields\n        for field in [\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"]:\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field: {field}\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        n_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if not isinstance(n_tokens, int) or n_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / n_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"gain\": round(gain, 8),\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\n            \"parseable\": parseable,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_ids,\n        \"total_accepted\": len(accepted_ids),\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nNow let me verify with the test cases:\n\nCase 0 (threshold=0.05):\n- call0: gain=1.94835097-0.38569502=1.56265595, norm=1.56265595/5=0.31253119, parseable=True -\u003e accepted\n- call1: gain=1.06116273-0.68319969=0.37796304, norm=0.37796304/4=0.09449076, parseable=True -\u003e accepted\n- call2: gain=1.21810502-0.47260371=0.74550131, norm=0.74550131/6=0.12425022, parseable=True -\u003e accepted\n- call3: gain=1.05721833-0.29767903=0.7595393, norm=0.7595393/5=0.1519078...6, parseable=True -\u003e accepted\n- call4: gain=1.06717367-0.85733566=0.20983801, norm=0.20983801/5=0.0419676..., parseable=True -\u003e gain \u003c threshold? 0.0419676 \u003c 0.05, so REJECTED\n- call5: gain=1.66191711-0.89798497=0.76393214, norm=0.76393214/4=0.19098303..., parseable=True -\u003e accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5\n\nCase 2 (threshold=0.05):\n- call4 is not parseable -\u003e rejected regardless\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me now format this as the required JSON response.\n\nActually wait - the response format must be exactly one JSON object. No markdown. Let me construct this properly.\n\nThe implementation needs to be a JSON string. Let me finalize it and make sure it's clean.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the rounding. The task says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I'll round to reasonable precision, maybe 8 decimal places to preserve precision while still being \"rounded.\"\n\nLet me now write the final JSON response. The implementation value is the Python source as a JSON string with proper escaping.\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be numeric\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    required_fields = {\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"}\n    \n    accepted_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        missing = required_fields - set(call.keys())\n        if missing:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing required fields: {missing}\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        n_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if not isinstance(n_tokens, int) or n_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for call {call_id}\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"loss_without_call must be numeric for call {call_id}\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"loss_with_call must be numeric for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / n_tokens\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"gain\": round(gain, 8),\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\n            \"parseable\": bool(parseable),\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_ids,\n        \"total_accepted\": len(accepted_ids),\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. Now let me format it as JSON. The requirement says no markdown, just the JSON object.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be numeric\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    required_fields = {\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"}\\n\\n    accepted_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        missing = required_fields - set(call.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required fields: {missing}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        n_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(n_tokens, int) or n_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for call {call_id}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_without_call must be numeric for call {call_id}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_with_call must be numeric for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        # stronger counterfactual: gain from having the call\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        # normalize by prediction token count\\n        normalized_gain = gain / n_tokens\\n\\n        # inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"gain\\\": round(gain, 8),\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\\n            \\\"parseable\\\": bool(parseable),\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_ids,\\n        \\\"total_accepted\\\": len(accepted_ids),\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01h0vCYTtRNWcRHnajhRnLq2","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2054,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":35,"output_tokens":2275,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1695},"service_tier":"standard"}}